<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36022" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phĭlippŏpŏlis</span></b> ,
			ĕos (acc. -in or -im;
			abl. -i), f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φιλιππόπολις</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A city of Thrace on the Hebrus</i>, now <i>Philippopoli</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv.
				39, 53, 13 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 3, 38</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 11,
				18, § 41</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Amm. 26, 10,
			4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A city of Palestine</i>, perh. <i>the
				ruins of Ghereyah</i>, <i><span class="en">Aur.
				Vict. Caes. 28, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
